# Risk acceptance - reviewed 2026-11-03.
# Group 1 (expires 2027-01-31): fixed ONLY in Spring Framework 7.0.9; no 6.2.x release contains the fix, and the project runs
# Spring Boot 3.5 (Framework 6.2). Revisit when migrating to Spring Boot 4 / Spring Framework 7.
# Per the advisory titles the affected features are not used by this application - verify before relying on this:
#   CVE-2026-47884: spring-webmvc XsltView path limitation (the app renders no XSLT views)
#   CVE-2026-47892: WebFlux functional endpoints (spring-webflux is used only for the WebClient, there is no reactive server)
#   CVE-2026-47890: SSE stream corruption with view fragments (SSE frames are JSON written by SseEmitter, no server-rendered view fragments)
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-01-31
CVE-2026-47892 exp:2027-01-31
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-01-31
#
# Group 2 (expires 2026-12-15, deliberately short): fixed only in Tomcat 10.1.58 / 11.0.25 / 9.0.121; 10.1.58 is not on Maven Central yet.
# Per the advisory titles they concern Tomcat's own container-managed security (security constraints, DIGEST and FORM authenticators);
# this application authenticates with JWT through Spring Security and defines no Tomcat realm or security constraints - verify before relying on this.
# Action: as soon as 10.1.58 resolves on Maven Central, add <tomcat.version>10.1.58</tomcat.version> to backend/pom.xml and delete these lines.
CVE-2026-65182 exp:2026-12-15
